The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    protected function resolvePrimitive(ReflectionParameter $parameter)
    {
        if (! is_null($concrete = $this->getContextualConcrete('$'.$parameter->getName()))) {
            return Util::unwrapIfClosure($concrete, $this);
        }

        if ($parameter->isDefaultValueAvailable()) {
            return $parameter->getDefaultValue();
        }

        $this->unresolvablePrimitive($parameter);
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `Illuminate\Tests\Container\ContainerResolveNonInstantiableTest::testResolveVariadicPrimitive`:
            
```php
    public function testResolveVariadicPrimitive()
    {
        $container = new Container;
        $parent = $container->make(VariadicPrimitive::class);

        $this->assertSame($parent->params, []);
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Unresolvable dependency resolving [Parameter #0 [ <optional> ...$params ]] in class Illuminate\Tests\Container\VariadicPrimitive
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
protected function resolvePrimitive(ReflectionParameter $parameter)
{
    if (! is_null($concrete = $this->getContextualConcrete('$'.$parameter->getName()))) {
        return Util::unwrapIfClosure($concrete, $this);
    }

    if ($parameter->isDefaultValueAvailable()) {
        return $parameter->getDefaultValue();
    }

    // Check if the parameter is variadic and has no default value, it should return an empty array
    if ($parameter->isVariadic()) {
        return [];
    }

    $this->unresolvablePrimitive($parameter);
}
```
